  setInterval(() => {
    this.seconds += 1;
    console.log(this.seconds);
  }, 1000);
}
```

2. Store `this` in a separate variable before passing the callback (the older JavaScript approach):
```javascript
start() {
  const self = this;
  setInterval(function () {
    self.seconds += 1;
    console.log(self.seconds);
  }, 1000);
}
```

3. Use `.bind(this)` to explicitly attach `this` to the function:
```javascript
setInterval(function () {
  this.seconds += 1;
  console.log(this.seconds);
}.bind(this), 1000);
```

Among these approaches, the arrow function solution is the most straightforward and follows modern JavaScript conventions.

