  const data = await res.json();
  if (!data?.name) {
    throw new Error(`Profile for user ${userId} has no name`);
  }
  return data.name.toUpperCase();
}
```

This version correctly awaits the fetch, checks the HTTP status, validates the response shape, and allows callers to handle errors via try/catch since the function is `async`.

